add('3.1.3', True, ACCESS + ' Missing credentials, keyring errors, rejected refresh tokens and authorization errors fail closed. A failed outgoing-password read no longer falls back to the incoming password.', [(PROVIDERS,'fn stored_passwords(',20),(API,'match oauth::refresh(',13)], 'Provider error-mapping tests and disconnected-client tests passed; source shows no unauthenticated fallback.')
add('3.1.4', True, 'There is no public Overlook CRUD API. User-controlled identifiers/search inputs reach provider clients, where Google validates the bearer token’s ownership and scope. Gmail paths use users/me; Calendar and People APIs enforce their own sharing/ownership rules. Local SQLite queries for conversations/search bind account IDs. The local profile is a single OS-user trust boundary, not a multi-user service. Native source evidence is supplied for assessor scope review.', [(API,'pub const API_BASE',3),(STORE,'pub fn messages_in_conversation(',9),(STORE,'pub fn search(',15)])
add('3.1.5', True, 'The browser-facing sensitive endpoint is the transient OAuth callback. It is bound to 127.0.0.1 on a random port; a valid GET /callback, exact Host authority, matching per-attempt state and unambiguous parameters are required before the listener consumes a response. PKCE S256 binds code exchange. There are no cookie-authenticated state-changing web endpoints. Untrusted mail cannot navigate or submit forms in the isolated renderer.', [(SIGNIN,'fn validated_callback',18),(OAUTH,'pub fn random_state',5)], 'Forged state, wrong Host/path/method, duplicate Host/state and callback pollution regression tests passed. This is native regression evidence, not a general web DAST report.')
add('3.1.6', False, 'Overlook operates no document-root HTTP server, hosted directory listing, or public web application. Its only HTTP listener accepts a fixed loopback /callback route during sign-in and rejects other paths; it never serves local directories. Local files are not exposed by a browser server.', [(SIGNIN,'fn validated_callback',18)])
add('3.2.1', True, 'Google sign-in uses Authorization Code with PKCE S256 in the external system browser and a loopback redirect. A fresh 48-byte random verifier and 24-byte state are generated per attempt. The token exchange sends grant_type=authorization_code and code_verifier. No implicit or resource-owner-password flow is implemented.', [(OAUTH,'pub fn random()',12),(OAUTH,'params.insert("response_type"',9),(OAUTH,'pub fn token_request_body',15)], 'RFC 7636 Appendix B challenge test and authorization URL/callback tests passed.')
add('3.2.2', True, 'The redirect is constructed from the bound 127.0.0.1 ephemeral port and fixed /callback path; it is not accepted from untrusted input. The listener verifies method, path, one exact Host header and state, rejecting duplicates or mixed code/error responses before consumption. Token exchange sends the same redirect URI and original PKCE verifier. There is no response-driven redirect destination.', [(SIGNIN,'pub fn start(',15),(SIGNIN,'fn validated_callback',18)], 'Callback regression rejects mismatched state, duplicate parameters, wrong Host/method/path and duplicate Host headers.')
add('3.3.1', False, 'Overlook has no exposed administrative interface, admin accounts, privileged web console or hosted application backend. All application settings are local to the OS user. Google Account authentication is external, with MFA governed by Google/user policy. This N/A determination concerns application-exposed administrative interfaces; it does not attest to MFA settings on the developer’s Google Cloud or Cloudflare accounts.', [(SIGNIN,'pub fn start(',18),(PROVIDERS,'pub fn providers_for(',17)])
add('4.1.1', True, 'Off-device Google OAuth/API, update, autoconfiguration, and remote mail-resource requests enforce HTTPS. Remote IMAP/POP3/SMTP require implicit TLS or mandatory STARTTLS before credentials; plaintext is allowed only for explicit loopback endpoints. Rustls defaults support TLS 1.2/1.3. The native OAuth loopback callback is HTTP by the installed-app protocol; it is not an Internet service. No hosted Overlook TLS server exists for SSL Labs. TAC should assess the desktop client’s outbound TLS controls.', [(API,'let agent: ureq::Agent',9),(TLS,'fn tls_config(',12),(ENGINE,'if url.as_str().len()',13)], 'Full suite and actual TLS-backed synthetic resource/Chromium consent tests passed. No SSL Labs report is claimed for this desktop executable.')
add('4.1.2', True, 'Production mail and HTTPS clients use Rustls with public WebPKI trust roots and hostname verification. IMAP TLS completes its handshake before authentication and returns errors on certificate/protocol failures; no accept-invalid-certificate switch is implemented. The test suite’s synthetic certificate is trusted only in cfg(test) fixtures, never in the production client.', [(TLS,'fn tls_config(',12),(TLS,'pub(crate) fn wrap_tls',9),(SMTP,'fn connect(',24)], 'TLS-backed synthetic resource tests passed. Provider/public-CA validation is delegated to the patched Rustls/WebPKI libraries. No SSL Labs scan of a desktop client is asserted.')
add('4.1.3', True, 'Cryptographic uses: PKCE SHA-256 with a freshly generated 48-byte random verifier and 24-byte state; TLS 1.2/1.3 via Rustls with its secure default suites and ephemeral handshake keys; SHA-256 release-file integrity checks; OS-managed encrypted credential storage. Overlook does not implement its own encrypted mail database or application MAC/IV/key-rotation scheme. TLS keys/nonces are library-managed; vault encryption/keys/unlock policy are OS keyring-managed. OAuth token lifetime is provider-managed.', [(OAUTH,'pub fn random()',12),(TLS,'fn tls_config(',12),(UPDATER,'pub fn sha256_file',12)], 'PKCE RFC vector and SHA-256 known-vector tests passed. Patched crypto dependencies have zero known vulnerability advisories in the current RustSec scan; maintenance warnings are documented.')
add('4.1.4', True, 'TLS setup/handshake errors stop the connection before credentials are sent; certificate/protocol failures propagate as rejected operations. Keyring read/write/decryption failures become VaultError and do not trigger plaintext fallback. Overlook exposes no decryption API or network endpoint that reveals padding errors. TLS record cryptography and vault error handling are delegated to the respective libraries/OS service.', [(TLS,'pub(crate) fn wrap_tls',9),(VAULT,'pub fn load_secret',12),(PROVIDERS,'fn stored_passwords(',20)])
add('5.1.1', True, 'The only inbound HTTP query parser is the loopback OAuth callback. Recognized parameter names are URL-decoded and duplicate code/state/error fields are rejected, including encoded aliases. Mixed code+error, missing/wrong state, wrong method/path/Host and duplicate Host headers are rejected. Outbound query values are encoded before use. No public Overlook HTTP application/API exists.', [(OAUTH,'pub fn parse_callback',31),(SIGNIN,'fn validated_callback',18)], 'OAuth callback pollution/forgery regression tests passed. Native targeted tests are supplied; a hosted-app DAST scan was not performed.')
add('5.1.2', True, 'Overlook has no server-side redirect/forward endpoint. The loopback callback returns a fixed completion page. Mail documents cannot automatically navigate: href values are isolated for host hit-testing, scripts/forms/frames are removed or disabled, and external links require a user action to open in the system browser. Remote resource redirects are limited to five hops, HTTPS, public resolved IPs, allowed ports/types, and no embedded credentials; private targets and downgrade redirects are rejected.', [(ENGINE,'// No live navigation URL',11),(ENGINE,'if visited.len() > 5',17)], 'Real Chromium consent/redirect test and anonymous resource-fetch tests passed. This is native control evidence; external destinations intentionally opened by users are outside the renderer.')
add('5.1.3', True, 'The mail renderer’s host uses fixed CDP evaluation scripts for DOM preparation/measurement and input hit-testing. Untrusted HTML is passed as serde_json-serialized data to DOMParser, not concatenated as executable JavaScript. Scripts, forms, frames and event handlers are stripped, page script execution is disabled, and all external fetches are intercepted. No user-authored eval or executable template feature exists.', [(ENGINE,'let args = serde_json',17),(ENGINE,'"Emulation.setScriptExecutionDisabled"',7)], 'Real Chromium test confirmed injected scripts did not execute and unsafe elements were removed; adversarial document tests passed.')
add('5.1.4', True, 'There is no server-side template engine accepting user expressions. Native UI renders text values; generated HTML escapes user-controlled headers, and untrusted message HTML goes through structural sanitization. The isolated browser receives HTML as JSON-serialized data rather than interpolated executable code. Fixed print-page scripting does not evaluate user content.', [(UI,'subject = escape_html(&message.subject)',4),(ENGINE,'let args = serde_json',17),(SANITIZE,'builder.rm_tags(',12)], 'HTML formatting/adversarial document tests and real Chromium isolation test passed.')
add('5.1.5', True, 'Overlook has no hosted SSRF endpoint, but untrusted email resource fetches are treated as an SSRF-equivalent risk to the local device. Chromium is network-isolated. Explicitly consented resources are fetched by a separate anonymous HTTPS client without auth/cookie/referrer or proxy inheritance. PublicResolver filters actual connection IPs (including redirects), rejecting loopback/private/link-local/metadata/documentation ranges. Limits cover ports, MIME types, size, timeout and redirect count. User-configured mail servers are a separate intentional connection path.', [(ENGINE,'struct PublicResolver',20),(ENGINE,'if url.as_str().len()',13),(ENGINE,'// A fresh GET per hop',12)], 'Actual TLS resource tests and real Chromium consent tests verified consent gating, no identifying headers, private-redirect denial, and safe redirect handling.')
add('5.1.6', False, 'Overlook has no XPath engine, XML query interface, or DTD/external-entity resolver. The limited ISPDB autoconfiguration XML is scanned as text for fixed tag names over HTTPS; it does not evaluate XPath, expand DTDs, or fetch entities. Email HTML/SVG is handled by the isolated/sanitized rendering paths. Thus an XML/XPath injection endpoint is absent.', [(AUTOCONFIG,'fn elements(',17),(AUTOCONFIG,'fn unescape(',3)])
add('5.1.7', True, 'Received HTML is untrusted. Ammonia allowlists remove executable elements, event handlers, forms/frames and unsafe schemes; inline CSS is restricted. The isolated browser additionally disables page scripts and applies CSP, DOM filtering and network interception. User header text in generated pages is HTML-escaped. Ammonia was updated to 4.2.4 for the current CSS URL filtering advisory.', [(SANITIZE,'builder.rm_tags(',18),(BROWSER,'const CSP:',1),(ENGINE,'"Emulation.setScriptExecutionDisabled"',7)], 'Adversarial HTML/CSS tests and real Chromium script-injection checks passed; current RustSec scan reports no known vulnerabilities.')
add('5.1.8', True, 'SQLite queries use bound rusqlite parameters for account IDs, mail IDs, user text and search expressions. Dynamic SQL fragments are selected by application code rather than supplied as user SQL. Full-text search uses a bound MATCH value and bound account ID. No network-accessible database or SQL query API is exposed.', [(STORE,'pub fn search(',15),(STORE,'pub fn set_focus_rule(',17)], 'Store suite passed, including search, account-scoped queries and transactional operations. Evidence is source plus native tests, not a web DAST scan.')
add('5.1.9', True, 'Application subprocesses use Rust Command with separate arguments. The updater’s terminal fallback now uses a constant bash script and passes the package path as positional $1, quoted at use; package filenames are not interpolated into shell program text. Mail HTML does not execute commands. The browser helper is a local executable with fixed isolation flags.', [(UPDATER,'// Pass the path as an argument',19),(ENGINE,'let mut cmd = Command::new(executable)',12)], 'Source review and workspace checks passed. No live privileged installation was performed as part of evidence collection.')
add('5.1.10', True, 'No server-side include/file-include endpoint exists. The mail renderer blocks file/javascript navigation, strips frames/objects, and intercepts all resource fetches. Remote resources require public HTTPS. Downloaded attachment names replace directory separators/NUL and neutralize leading-dot names; destinations are constructed below the account/message attachment directory. User-selected local attachments/backups are intentional local file operations, not server includes.', [(UI,'fn attachment_path(',7),(ENGINE,'fn safe_link(',8),(ENGINE,'if url.as_str().len()',13)], 'Real Chromium injected file-frame and unsafe-element checks passed; resource policy rejects file URLs and private targets.')
add('5.2.1', True, 'There is no hosted upload directory or server-side execution path. As a mail client, Overlook intentionally supports arbitrary user-selected attachments; they are MIME-encoded/sent as data. Received attachments are stored as files under sanitized names and are not automatically executed. Inline previews are limited to supported image/PDF paths; external opening requires explicit user action. Remote renderer resources have MIME/size/port restrictions. Overlook does not claim antivirus scanning of attachments.', [(UI,'fn attachment_path(',7),(UI,'match after {',12),(ENGINE,'let allowed = match kind',22)], 'Source review plus mail/attachment and browser isolation tests. Applicability reflects a desktop mail client, not a generic hosted file-upload service.')
add('6.1.1', True, 'A RustSec cargo-audit 0.22.2 scan of Cargo.lock initially found seven vulnerability advisories. Updated ammonia 4.2.3→4.2.4, rustls 0.23.45→0.23.46, rustls-webpki 0.103.15→0.103.16, and webpki-roots 1.0.9→1.0.10. Re-scan reports zero known vulnerabilities. Eight transitive unmaintained-package warnings remain disclosed, not suppressed. This covers Rust dependencies; the installed Chromium, PDF tools and OS libraries require distribution security updates. TAC must confirm scanner acceptance and any required native/OS inventory coverage.', [('llm-docs/casa/logs/dependency-summary.txt','Scan:',30)], 'RustSec database commit 640bf5a9f06e66d8721e8772766531fe77c8630d, updated 2026-10-22. Full before/after JSON is retained in the evidence bundle.')
add('6.2.1', True, 'Release packaging builds cargo --release --locked; Rust release debug assertions are disabled by default. No production web debug console or TCP DevTools endpoint is exposed. The optional renderer uses a private pipe and private runtime directory. Diagnostic logging can be requested locally through RUST_LOG, but protocol/vault logging is unconditionally filtered to prevent wire-secret disclosure even at trace level. This is a desktop production-mode assessment, not a hosted web debug scan.', [('.github/workflows/release.yml','- name: Build release binary',3),(ENGINE,'"--host-resolver-rules',10),(MAIN,'fn safe_log_metadata',3)], 'Release build and native runtime isolation checks are recorded separately. Source reviewed for pipe-only browser debugging.')
